"It's neither sympathy\nNor cultural\nNeither pure, nor impure\nBut purely natural.\n\nYes the blood is real\nAnd it's not to be ashamed of\nYes there's pain and cramps\nBut it cannot make your work stop!\n\nYes there are pads and cups\nAnd many electric tools\nYes they are pretty normal\nUntill 'n unless you belong to the fools.\n\nYes there are pills\nAnd they're pretty deadly too!\nJust to hide for the sake of tradition\nFoolishness become a part of you!\n\nKitchen can't be restricted,\nTemples don't go unholy.\nBlack bags bring in shame for real,\nAnd give her mine a melancholy.\n\nNo it ain't a mockery arsenal,\nNot something to make joke of,\nWe mustn't turn it into slur,\nCuz it's neither pejorative, nor scoff!\n\nFriends should know about it,\nBrothers should be taught.\nFathers must not command to hide,\nCuz it's something to be open about!"